# One recorded conversation with the core, replayed by `gmx plugin test
# --offline .`. `core` lines are written to the plugin's stdin; `plugin` lines
# must appear on its stderr, in this order, as a subset of the real line. "*"
# matches any value.
#
# No core, no socket and no clock: GMX_RPC is empty, so there is no programme
# to direct. The interesting line is the `explain` call, which runs the whole
# rule set against a state the transcript carries and answers with the take it
# would have made.
